                <pb facs="0089" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00/481: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-01T14:00:00+03:25">October 1, 1938—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 1—12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>103. Referring to the Department’s circular telegram September 27, 4 p.m., in the
                    event of a general European war there appears to be no reason to expect
                    immediate disturbances in Persia or new difficulties except possibly of a
                    financial or economic nature.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
